{"analyst_worksheet":{"steps":["1. Read data_quality.missing_data_flags first. Resolve every flag whose `needs_analyst_research` is true by web research, citing the source and its timestamp (confirmed QB, injuries, late weather).","2. Read football.matchup_comparison and schedules.json: weigh opponent-adjusted offense vs the ACTUAL opposing defense, discount stats built on weak schedules, and do not over-weight last-3 form.","3. Read game_script: the dominant, competitive and upset scripts, and what evidence would flip each.","4. Use distributions.json for shape and spread (reference-class frequencies, closest games, the baseline's real error). Do not invent a score and assume a normal curve.","5. Write YOUR probability and an uncertainty range for each thesis you will price (winner, cover, total, team totals, halves, quarters, ladders). Keep them football-derived: never copy Kalshi's implied probability.","6. Compare every listed contract of the relevant families (markets.json) on the side you would buy, at the NO ask for NO, with the all-in cost. Use bet-up-to prices from your LOWER bound. A stake is optional, advisory and yours: leave it unsized unless you can justify it (max 5U, 1U = $75).","7. Reconcile correlated exposure across contracts and games, then return one ranked card. Passing is a correct answer."],"your_output_per_game":{"confirmed_inputs":{"injuries":null,"qb":null,"sources":[],"weather":null},"evidence_tier":"ANALYST_JUDGMENT","family_estimates":"for every family you price: the probability (low/point/high) of each thesis, and the contracts that express it","projected_score":"home/away points with a range (not a point estimate)","script_probabilities":{"competitive":null,"dominant":null,"upset":null},"winner_probability":{"high":null,"low":null,"point":null}}},"availability":{"absence_effect_guide":"for each confirmed absence: which unit (QB, OL, front seven, secondary, skill) -> which row of football.matchup_comparison it touches -> widen your ran